    "body": "<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/developing-today/code/pull/7860?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\" alt=\"Explain Change →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> ## Review failed\n> \n> The pull request is closed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: failure by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\nThis pull request adds a decision record for benchmark regression gates. It documents comparison requirements, metric verdicts, waivers, baseline updates, and result retention. It also adds the record to two documentation indexes.\n\n**Changes: Benchmark regression gates**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Comparison and verdict rules** <br> `doc/2026-11-08T23-45-30Z_design_id5897_regression_gates/2026-11-08T23-45-30Z_design_id5897_regression_gates.md`, `doc/README.md`, `planning/architecture/README.md`|The decision record defines comparison identity, metric budgets, paired-run sampling and verdicts, measurement states, and programme boundaries. It states that throughput and p95 latency are initially blocking. The documentation indexes link to the record.|\n|**Waivers and baseline updates** <br> `doc/2026-11-08T23-45-30Z_design_id5897_regression_gates/2026-11-08T23-45-30Z_design_id5897_regression_gates.md`|The record defines waiver scope, approval, and expiry rules. It also specifies reviewed, versioned baseline updates.|\n|**Run archive** <br> `doc/2026-11-08T23-45-30Z_design_id5897_regression_gates/2026-11-08T23-45-30Z_design_id5897_regression_gates.md`|The record designates monthly GitHub Releases for completed run bundles and accepted baseline versions. It specifies that archive-write failure leaves a run incomplete.|\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Estimated code review effort:** 2 (Simple) | ~12 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"077b882c9b41de3ea4599f04ffc67e3c3f4b4c85\" -->\n**Change:** Other\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n**Possibly related issues**\n\n- `developing-today/code#5897` — The decision record covers the issue’s requested design topics, but the supplied context says the pull request does not close the issue.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-low-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Low</strong> · up to <code>077b8</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **🔵 Low** · up to `077b8`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"077b882c9b41de3ea4599f04ffc67e3c3f4b4c85\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"077b882c9b41de3ea4599f04ffc67e3c3f4b4c85\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThis PR adds a design record for benchmark regression gates and links it from two indexes. It changes no runtime behavior. The record should say how a measured cell with a missing blocking metric is reported, so a future gate cannot pass it silently. This is a small wording fix to make before or soon after merge.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n\n\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=developing-today/code&utm_content=7860)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Share</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->",
